    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`--constrained-json-disable-any-whitespace` is documented as \"Enforce compact representation in JSON constrained output\". The xgrammar backend turns it into `compile_json_schema(any_whitespace=False)` without `separators`, so xgrammar falls back to the `json.dumps` default `(\", \", \": \")`, and the grammar *requires* a space after every `,` and `:`.\n\nAcceptance of each output for the schema `{\"a\": integer, \"b\": [integer]}`:\n\n| `any_whitespace` | `separators` | `{\"a\":1,\"b\":[2,3]}` | `{\"a\": 1, \"b\": [2, 3]}` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `False` | `None` (today) | rejected | accepted |\n| `False` | `(\",\", \":\")` (this PR) | accepted | rejected |\n| `True` | `None` | accepted | accepted |\n\nThese were checked on xgrammar 0.1.32 and 0.2.1. In the 0.2.1 sources, `JSONSchemaConverter` picks `\", \"` and `\": \"` when `separators` is unset, `any_whitespace` is false, and there is no indent.\n\nThe llguidance backend already emits compact JSON for this flag. It passes `whitespace_flexible=False`, and `JsonCompileOptions` defaults to `\",\"` and `\":\"`. With llguidance 1.7.0 and those options, `{\"a\":1,\"b\":[2,3]}` is accepted and `{\"a\": 1, \"b\": [2, 3]}` is rejected.\n\nThose separators tokenize at roughly one token per character. On a JSON-heavy workload we measured them at about 12% of output tokens.\n\n## Modifications\n\nPass `separators=(\",\", \":\")` to `compile_json_schema` when `any_whitespace` is `False`. The default (`any_whitespace=True`) and the builtin `$$ANY$$` JSON grammar are unchanged.\n\n**Behavior change:** with the flag set, xgrammar outputs become `{\"a\":1}` instead of `{\"a\": 1}`. That is what the flag's help text describes, it matches llguidance, and the output is still valid JSON. The constrained-decoding test sets the flag in AMD CI; its JSON checks parse the output with `json.loads`, so they are unaffected.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nGrammar acceptance is shown in the table above. End to end, a JSON-schema structured-output replay workload on an out-of-tree platform passes with the flag set.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Formatting: black-stable (ruff-format compatible), imports in isort order.\n- [x] Unit test: `test/registered/unit/constrained/test_xgrammar_backend.py` builds a real `XGrammarGrammarBackend` with a character-level tokenizer and checks the flag against compact and spaced JSON. It fails before this change and passes after.\n",
